@techreport{CheesemanBennett1955,
  author      = {Cheeseman, I. C. and Bennett, W. E.},
  title       = {The Effect of Ground on a Helicopter Rotor in Forward Flight},
  institution = {Aeronautical Research Council},
  address     = {London, U.K.},
  type        = {R\&M},
  number      = {3021},
  year        = {1955}
}
The nominal DT described above reproduces the vehicle dynamics and the aerodynamic correction for forward flight, but it does not account for the additional rotor--surface interaction generated as the vehicle crosses the finite obstacle. We introduce this interaction through a deliberately low-order physical model inspired by the analytical formulation of Cheeseman and Bennett for an isolated rotor~\cite{CheesemanBennett1955}.